+### One file for content and code (server mods)
+
+A server mod (`api = "0.3"`, `side = "server"`) may also list `registries` and carry `assets/` and `data/` next to its
+`mod.wasm`: one `.hmod` adds the mod's blocks, items, menu screens and renderers **and** runs its code. The blocks'
+ids are `<id>:<name>` (the file's folder is `data/<id>/horizon/`), so the mod's id is the namespace its blocks have.
+`cargo horizon-mod build` in a folder with a `Cargo.toml` and `data/` packs both; `check` and `test` run on the
+result. The game reads the content once at start (turn the mod on before opening the world), and starts the code with
+the world. A client half (keys, a HUD) is a separate client mod, which `net-client` joins to it.
+
 ### Content mods (API 0.2)
 
 A content mod has capability `registries` and carries `assets/` and `data/` in the `.hmod`. It adds blocks and items
